      "content": "i know... people say that stuff but it doesn't change the reality. it's like i'm a ghost haunting my own life. i go through the motions, i eat, i sleep, but it all feels so hollow because the \"me\" that mattered to people is just gone. the version of me that was part of a group, a friend, a person... that person died when they all left. i'm just the leftovers. it feels more honest to just be gone than to keep pretending i'm still part of the world.",
